                "In Part 5, we engineer an Anti-Pattern Dead Equity Cap Table Drag Simulator in Python. We will model the capitalization collapse of an unvested founder resignation, simulate corporate recapitalization and emergency equity restructurings, calculate the resulting ownership dilution across remaining active founders, and trigger automated legal risk alerts when dead equity exceeds the ten percent fatal threshold. Corporate governance history demonstrates that unresolved dead equity destroys promising software ventures far more frequently than technological failure or market competition. Implementing ironclad reverse vesting covenants and statutory repurchase protections ensures that every single share of company common stock remains actively deployed in the service of ongoing enterprise value creation, insulating the startup against dead equity paralysis and guaranteeing that equity ownership reflects active operational contribution throughout the company entire commercial existence and shielding founding partners from devastating cap table drag across every stage of technological venture growth."
